  "notes": "Space Shuttle L-7 gameplay with direct public switch writes only (keyboard handling and the driver's simulator stay off). Three balls rest on ball ramp switches 10, 11 and 12 and attract mode is observed for 20 s; a coin and the credit button start a game and the ROM serves a ball with the ball-ramp release (2) from position 12 into the shooter lane (36). Jet and kicker switches show PinMAME's switch-driven special solenoids, 82 and 84 show the flipper column copy into 41 and the synthetic 45-48, the right outlane rollover and the 3-bank show the outlane gate (13) and the 3-bank reset (6), the ramp bull's-eye resets the T drop target (5), a ball resting in each eject hole (16, 24) is locked and the ROM serves the next ball, the long-ramp shot (32) fires both eject holes (3, 4) for multi-ball, the remaining scoring switches are closed once, the three balls drain through the outhole (1) back to the ball ramp and the ROM serves ball 2, and three playfield-tilt closures tilt the ball. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
